lt on them, not like
// a bystander's glance. The verb is the same, the social weight is not.
func (s *TurnService) applyTransform(ctx context.Context, tc *turnContext, evt *event.GameEvent, v *verdict, deed string) {
	hazard := entity.IsHazardEffect(v.effect)
	if s.mutator != nil {
		note := entity.EffectNote(v.effect)
		if _, err := s.mutator.ApplyEffect(ctx, v.targetEnt.ID, v.effect, note, tc.tick); err != nil {
			s.logger.Warn("transform mutation failed", zap.String("entity", v.targetEnt.Name), zap.Error(err))
		}
	}

	// A neutral, harmless change earns a glance and a memory, nothing heavier.
	if !v.hostile && !hazard {
		for _, w := range tc.coLocated() {
			s.formMemory(ctx, tc, evt, w, fmt.Sprintf("%s на моих глазах: «%s»", tc.player.Identity.Name, deed))
		}
		return
	}

	playerName := tc.player.Identity.Name
	// The owner of the ruined thing, if standing right here, is the personally
	// wronged party — handled apart from the onlookers, as applyHostility handles
	// an assault's victim. An absent owner's grievance on later discovery is a
	// future mechanic, as it is on the take-path.
	var ownerID *domain.ActorID
	if id := s.ownerOf(ctx, v.targetEnt); id != nil {
		if owner := tc.actorByID(*id); owner != nil && owner.GetCurrentLocation() == tc.player.GetCurrentLocation() {
			ownerID = id
		}
	}

	for _, w := range tc.coLocated() {
		if ownerID != nil && w.ID == *ownerID {
			continue // wronged personally below, not a mere onlooker
		}
		guard := isGuard(w)
		if s.behavior != nil {
			if guard {
				// The law hardens at a crime, it does not cower — resolve, not dread.
				s.applyImpulse(ctx, tc, w, map[actor.EmotionType]float32{actor.EmotionAnger: 0.65})
			} else {
				s.applyImpulse(ctx, tc, w, map[actor.EmotionType]float32{actor.EmotionFear: 0.6, actor.EmotionAnxiety: 0.5})
			}
		}
		// A hazard (arson) leaves a bystander LASTING fear of the player, exactly as a
		// blow does — otherwise the city forgets the arsonist the moment the flames die;
		// the catalogue carries that fear for a non-guard onlooker, zero for a guard (who
		// answers with resolve, not cowering) and zero for a harmless transform (a smashed
		// mug frightens no one into lasting fear). A guard's lasting mark is a lawman's
		// grievance, set apart on the same live relationship the delta then persists.
		if guard {
			actor.MarkCrimeWitnessed(w, tc.player.ID) // the law remembers — confronts on sight
		}
		s.applyRelDelta(ctx, tc, w, relationshipConsequence(roleHazardOnlooker, hazard, guard), "погром")
		mem := fmt.Sprintf("%s у всех на глазах решается на «%s» — и доводит дело до конца", playerName, deed)
		if guard {
			mem = fmt.Sprintf("На моих глазах преступление: %s — «%s»", playerName, deed)
		}
		s.formMemory(ctx, tc, evt, w, mem)
	}

	// The owner takes the full relationship damage and a lasting wariness of the
	// one who ruined their property — anger first (it is their loss), and the
	// world remembers it as personal, not as something they merely watched. A
	// GUARD owner is still the law: they harden into a confronting grievance
	// (anger, no cowering fear), not the dread a townsperson carries — otherwise
	// destroying a guard's own thing would make the watch trail off in fear,
	// against the «law hardens, it does not cower» invariant.
	if ownerID != nil {
		owner := tc.actorByID(*ownerID)
		guard := isGuard(owner)
		if s.behavior != nil {
			impulse := map[actor.EmotionType]float32{actor.EmotionAnger: 0.6, actor.EmotionFear: 0.4}
			if guard {
				impulse = map[actor.EmotionType]float32{actor.EmotionAnger: 0.65}
			}
			s.applyImpulse(ctx, tc, owner, impulse)
		}
		if guard {
			actor.MarkCrimeWitnessed(owner, tc.player.ID) // their own property ruined → a lawman's grievance, confront on sight
		}
		// The owner takes the full disposition damage and a lasting wariness — their
		// property wronged weighs like an assault (and a hazard endangers them bodily
		// too, so the catalogue floors their fear at the fleeing-onlooker's). A guard
		// owner is still the law: the catalogue zeroes their dread, the grievance above
		// stands instead.
		s.applyRelDelta(ctx, tc, owner, relationshipConsequence(rolePropertyOwner, hazard, guard), "порча имущества")
		s.formMemory(ctx, tc, evt, owner, fmt.Sprintf("%s уничтожает на моих глазах моё: %s", playerName, v.targetEnt.Name))
	}
}

// applyImpulse drives an NPC's emotions with floor semantics and persists the
// change; an EmotionChanged event keeps the log honest.
func (s *TurnService) applyImpulse(ctx context.Context, tc *turnContext, npc *actor.Actor, floors map[actor.EmotionType]float32) {
	if !s.behavior.ApplyEmotionImpulse(npc, floors) {
		return
	}
	if err := s.actors.Update(ctx, npc); err != nil {
		s.logger.Warn("persist emotion impulse failed", zap.String("npc", npc.Identity.Name), zap.Error(err))
	}
	dominant, intensity := npc.State.Emotional.CurrentTone.GetDominantEmotion()
	evt := event.NewGameEvent(
		event.EventTypeEmotionChanged,
		npc.ID, npc.State.GetCurrentLocation(), tc.worldID, tc.tick,
		event.StateChangeEventData{
			ActorID:   npc.ID,
			StateType: event.StateChangeEmotion,
			OldValue:  event.StringValue(""),
			NewValue:  event.StringValue(string(dominant)),
			Reason:    fmt.Sprintf("реакция на действие игрока (%.2f)", intensity),
		},
	)
	if err := s.events.Append(ctx, evt); err != nil {
		s.logger.Warn("append emotion change failed", zap.Error(err))
	}
}

// formMemory writes one actor's memory of the deed, coloured by how they feel
// right now (the impulse just landed). Best-effort: a failed memory must not
// fail the turn.
func (s *TurnService) formMemory(ctx context.Context, tc *turnContext, evt *event.GameEvent, owner *actor.Actor, perspective string) {
	if s.memory == nil {
		return
	}
	if _, err := s.memory.CreateFromEvent(ctx, evt, owner.ID, perspective, memory.EmotionalToneFromActor(owner)); err != nil {
		s.logger.Warn("memory formation failed", zap.String("npc", owner.Identity.Name), zap.Error(err))
	}
}

package turn

import (
	"context"
	"testing"

	"github.com/dnd-llm/dnd-llm/internal/domain"
	"github.com/dnd-llm/dnd-llm/internal/domain/actor"
	"github.com/dnd-llm/dnd-llm/internal/domain/entity"
)

// fakeHazards serves present entities per location.
type fakeHazards struct {
	byLoc map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity
}

func (f *fakeHazards) ListPresentAt(_ context.Context, _ domain.WorldID, loc domain.LocationID, _ []domain.ActorID) ([]*entity.Entity, error) {
	return f.byLoc[loc], nil
}

func (f *fakeHazards) HazardLocations(_ context.Context, _ domain.WorldID) ([]domain.LocationID, error) {
	var locs []domain.LocationID
	for loc, ents := range f.byLoc {
		for _, e := range ents {
			if e.StateText(entity.StateHazard) != "" {
				locs = append(locs, loc)
				break
			}
		}
	}
	return locs, nil
}

func burningThing() *entity.Entity {
	return &entity.Entity{
		ID:    domain.NewEntityID(),
		Name:  "Сруб «Лунного Брода»",
		State: map[string]any{entity.StateHazard: entity.EffectBurn},
	}
}

// TestApplyEnvironmentalHazards is the consume side of escalating destruction: a
// standing fire terrifies everyone in its location (recomputing escalation to
// Terrified, which drops their calm options downstream), while NPCs elsewhere
// are untouched and the player is left to their own turn.
func TestApplyEnvironmentalHazards(t *testing.T) {
	burning := domain.NewLocationID()
	safe := domain.NewLocationID()

	inFire := actorAt(burning)
	inFire.Type = actor.ActorTypeStoryNPC
	away := actorAt(safe)
	away.Type = actor.ActorTypeStoryNPC
	player := actorAt(burning)
	player.Type = actor.ActorTypePlayer
	byID := map[domain.ActorID]*actor.Actor{inFire.ID: inFire, away.ID: away, player.ID: player}

	p := &TickProcessor{
		behaviorSystem: actor.NewBehaviorSystem(),
		hazards: &fakeHazards{byLoc: map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity{
			burning: {burningThing()},
		}},
	}
	_, dirty, _ := p.displaceFromUntenable(context.Background(), domain.NewGameTime(), domain.WorldID("w"), byID)

	if !dirty[inFire.ID] {
		t.Fatal("an NPC in a burning place must be dirtied")
	}
	if got := inFire.State.Emotional.CurrentTone.Emotions[actor.EmotionFear]; got < hazardFearFloor {
		t.Errorf("fear floor = %.2f, want >= %.2f", got, hazardFearFloor)
	}
	if inFire.State.Emotional.EscalationLevel != actor.EscalationTerrified {
		t.Errorf("a burning place must terrify (so calm options drop), got %q", inFire.State.Emotional.EscalationLevel)
	}
	if dirty[away.ID] {
		t.Error("an NPC in a safe place must not be touched")
	}
	if dirty[player.ID] {
		t.Error("the player flees on their own turn, not via the tick")
	}
}

// A location with no standing hazard leaves everyone calm.
func TestApplyEnvironmentalHazards_NoHazard(t *testing.T) {
	loc := domain.NewLocationID()
	npc := actorAt(loc)
	npc.Type = actor.ActorTypeStoryNPC
	byID := map[domain.ActorID]*actor.Actor{npc.ID: npc}

	p := &TickProcessor{
		behaviorSystem: actor.NewBehaviorSystem(),
		hazards:        &fakeHazards{byLoc: map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity{}},
	}
	if _, dirty, _ := p.displaceFromUntenable(context.Background(), domain.NewGameTime(), domain.WorldID("w"), byID); len(dirty) != 0 {
		t.Errorf("no hazard must leave everyone calm, got %d dirtied", len(dirty))
	}
}

// fakeIgniter records which entities a spreading fire set alight and which it
// later consumed.
type fakeIgniter struct {
	lit    []domain.EntityID
	burned []domain.EntityID
}

func (f *fakeIgniter) Ignite(_ context.Context, id domain.EntityID, _ domain.Tick) error {
	f.lit = append(f.lit, id)
	return nil
}

func (f *fakeIgniter) BurnOut(_ context.Context, id domain.EntityID, _ domain.Tick) error {
	f.burned = append(f.burned, id)
	return nil
}

func flammableThing(name string, cat entity.Category) *entity.Entity {
	return &entity.Entity{ID: domain.NewEntityID(), Name: name, Category: cat}
}

// fakeKindler records the locations whose LATENT prop fund a fire reached.
type fakeKindler struct{ reached []domain.LocationID }

func (f *fakeKindler) KindleNext(_ context.Context, _ domain.WorldID, loc domain.LocationID, _ domain.Tick) (string, error) {
	f.reached = append(f.reached, loc)
	return "Свеча", nil
}

// TestSpreadFire: a standing blaze sets exactly ONE flammable neighbour alight
// (wood/cloth/food — never a drink); no fire, or no kindling, means no ignition.
func TestSpreadFire(t *testing.T) {
	loc := domain.NewLocationID()
	npc := actorAt(loc)
	npc.Type = actor.ActorTypeStoryNPC
	byID := map[domain.ActorID]*actor.Actor{npc.ID: npc}

	fire := burningThing()
	cloak := flammableThing("Тканый кусок", entity.CategoryClothing) // cloth burns
	bowl := flammableThing("Глиняная миска", entity.CategoryUtensil) // ceramic does NOT
	ale := flammableThing("Кружка эля", entity.CategoryDrink)        // liquids do not

	ig := &fakeIgniter{}
	p := &TickProcessor{
		hazards: &fakeHazards{byLoc: map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity{loc: {fire, bowl, cloak, ale}}},
		igniter: ig,
	}
	p.spreadFire(context.Background(), domain.NewGameTime(), domain.WorldID("w"), byID)
	if len(ig.lit) != 1 || ig.lit[0] != cloak.ID {
		t.Errorf("fire must spread to the cloth ONLY (not ceramic/ale), got %v", ig.lit)
	}

	// No standing hazard → nothing catches.
	ig2 := &fakeIgniter{}
	p2 := &TickProcessor{
		hazards: &fakeHazards{byLoc: map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity{loc: {cloak, ale}}},
		igniter: ig2,
	}
	p2.spreadFire(context.Background(), domain.NewGameTime(), domain.WorldID("w"), byID)
	if len(ig2.lit) != 0 {
		t.Errorf("no fire means no spread, got %v", ig2.lit)
	}
}

// TestSpreadFireReachesLatentPropFund: a blaze with no MATERIALIZED flammable
// neighbour falls through to the latent prop fund — the tavern's authored candle
// catches even though no entity for it exists yet. When a crystallized flammable
// IS present, that tier wins and the latent fund is left untouched.
func TestSpreadFireReachesLatentPropFund(t *testing.T) {
	loc := domain.NewLocationID()
	byID := map[domain.ActorID]*actor.Actor{}

	// Only the fire is present — every flammable thing of the place is still a
	// latent prop, so the present-entity tier finds no kindling.
	fire := burningThing()
	ig := &fakeIgniter{}
	kn := &fakeKindler{}
	p := &TickProcessor{
		hazards: &fakeHazards{byLoc: map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity{loc: {fire}}},
		igniter: ig,
		kindler: kn,
	}
	p.spreadFire(context.Background(), domain.NewGameTime(), domain.WorldID("w"), byID)
	if len(ig.lit) != 0 {
		t.Errorf("no materialized kindling — the present tier must ignite nothing, got %v", ig.lit)
	}
	if len(kn.reached) != 1 || kn.reached[0] != loc {
		t.Errorf("fire must reach the latent prop fund of the burning place, got %v", kn.reached)
	}

	// A crystallized flammable present → the present tier wins; the latent fund
	// is NOT reached (things already in play burn first).
	cloak := flammableThing("Тканый кусок", entity.CategoryClothing)
	ig2 := &fakeIgniter{}
	kn2 := &fakeKindler{}
	p2 := &TickProcessor{
		hazards: &fakeHazards{byLoc: map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity{loc: {fire, cloak}}},
		igniter: ig2,
		kindler: kn2,
	}
	p2.spreadFire(context.Background(), domain.NewGameTime(), domain.WorldID("w"), byID)
	if len(ig2.lit) != 1 || ig2.lit[0] != cloak.ID {
		t.Errorf("present flammable must burn first, got %v", ig2.lit)
	}
	if len(kn2.reached) != 0 {
		t.Errorf("latent fund must be left untouched while crystallized fuel remains, got %v", kn2.reached)
	}
}

// burningSince returns a thing alight since the given tick.
func burningSince(tick domain.Tick) *entity.Entity {
	return &entity.Entity{
		ID:    domain.NewEntityID(),
		Name:  "Табурет",
		State: map[string]any{entity.StateHazard: entity.EffectBurn, entity.StateHazardSince: uint64(tick)},
	}
}

// TestConsumeFire: a fire burns a thing out after fireBurnTicks (clearing the
// hazard); before that span it keeps burning; a hazard with no recorded ignition
// tick is left untouched (never silently consumed).
func TestConsumeFire(t *testing.T) {
	loc := domain.NewLocationID()
	old := burningSince(10)   // lit at 10 → consumed once tick ≥ 16
	fresh := burningSince(14) // lit at 14 → still burning at 15
	noStamp := burningThing() // pre-timestamp hazard → never auto-consumed
	byID := map[domain.ActorID]*actor.Actor{}

	// Just before the old thing's span elapses: nothing burns out.
	ig := &fakeIgniter{}
	p := &TickProcessor{
		hazards: &fakeHazards{byLoc: map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity{loc: {old, fresh, noStamp}}},
		igniter: ig,
	}
	p.consumeFire(context.Background(), domain.NewGameTimeAt(15), domain.WorldID("w"), byID)
	if len(ig.burned) != 0 {
		t.Errorf("nothing has burned long enough at tick 15, got %v", ig.burned)
	}

	// At tick 16 the old thing has burned its full span; the fresh one has not.
	ig2 := &fakeIgniter{}
	p2 := &TickProcessor{
		hazards: &fakeHazards{byLoc: map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity{loc: {old, fresh, noStamp}}},
		igniter: ig2,
	}
	p2.consumeFire(context.Background(), domain.NewGameTimeAt(16), domain.WorldID("w"), byID)
	if len(ig2.burned) != 1 || ig2.burned[0] != old.ID {
		t.Errorf("only the thing past its burn span must be consumed, got %v", ig2.burned)
	}
}

// carriedHazards models a thing NOT pinned to a place (no located_at, so absent
// from HazardLocations) but present in a holder's hands — surfaced by
// ListPresentAt only when that holder is passed.
type carriedHazards struct {
	pinned    []domain.LocationID
	carriedAt map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity
}

func (c *carriedHazards) HazardLocations(_ context.Context, _ domain.WorldID) ([]domain.LocationID, error) {
	return c.pinned, nil
}

func (c *carriedHazards) ListPresentAt(_ context.Context, _ domain.WorldID, loc domain.LocationID, holders []domain.ActorID) ([]*entity.Entity, error) {
	if len(holders) == 0 {
		return nil, nil // carried things are invisible without their holder
	}
	return c.carriedAt[loc], nil
}

// TestConsumeFire_CarriedFireBurnsOut is the regression for the eternal-hazard
// bug: a burning thing taken from a place loses its located_at pin, so it never
// appears in HazardLocations. Consumption must still burn it out — it watches the
// carried tier (like evacuation), not just the pinned tier (like spread). Without
// the holder-aware scan this thing would burn forever, flooding fear on its
// carrier's room every tick.
func TestConsumeFire_CarriedFireBurnsOut(t *testing.T) {
	loc := domain.NewLocationID()
	carrier := actorAt(loc)
	carrier.Type = actor.ActorTypePlayer
	byID := map[domain.ActorID]*actor.Actor{carrier.ID: carrier}

	torch := burningSince(10) // lit at 10, carried (no located_at pin)
	ig := &fakeIgniter{}
	p := &TickProcessor{
		hazards: &carriedHazards{
			pinned:    nil, // not pinned anywhere → HazardLocations is empty
			carriedAt: map[domain.LocationID][]*entity.Entity{loc: {torch}},
		},
		igniter: ig,
	}
	p.consumeFire(context.Background(), domain.NewGameTimeAt(16), domain.WorldID("w"), byID)
	if len(ig.burned) != 1 || ig.burned[0] != torch.ID {
		t.Errorf("a carried fire past its span must still burn out, got %v", ig.burned)
	}
}

